Just how much does a unit weigh in real-world terms?

We know that a plate mail in Nethack weighs 450 units.

According to http://www.hyw.com/Books/History/plate_ma.htm, the typical
plate mail was 70 pounds.

So 450 units = 70 pounds = 31.8 kilograms.

Therefore 1 unit = .071 kilograms, or 71 grams.

